#: ../../../reference/interfaces/snapd-control-interface.md:2
msgid "snapd-control interface"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/snapd-control-interface.md:4
msgid ""
"The `snapd-control` interface enables snap management, such as snap "
"installation, removal and refresh-control by communicating with the snapd "
"daemon."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/snapd-control-interface.md:6
msgid ""
"Due to its ability to permit the installation any snap at potentially any "
"confinement level, `snapd-control` is primarily intended to be used by "
"[brand store](https://documentation.ubuntu.com/core/explanation/stores/store-"
"overview/) owners as they will typically already have full access to their "
"devices."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/snapd-control-interface.md:8
msgid ""
"Consequently, consumers of this interface require {ref}`approval <interfaces-"
"process-for-aliases-auto-connections-and-tracks>` for distribution via the "
"Snap Store, and this approval is only likely to be given under strict and "
"specific circumstances."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/snapd-control-interface.md:11
msgid "Developer details"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/snapd-control-interface.md:14
msgid ""
"**{ref}`Auto-connect <explanation-interfaces-interface-auto-connection>`**: "
"no</br> **{ref}`Super-privileged <reference-operations-interfaces-super-"
"privileged-interfaces>`**: yes</br>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/snapd-control-interface.md:14
msgid "</br>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/snapd-control-interface.md:17
msgid "**Attributes** :"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/snapd-control-interface.md:18
msgid ""
"`refresh-schedule` (plug):  can be set to `managed` to signal an intention "
"to permit only manual refreshes for the snap:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/snapd-control-interface.md:20
msgid ""
"plugs:\n"
"    snapd:\n"
"        interface: snapd-control\n"
"        refresh-schedule: managed\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/snapd-control-interface.md:27
msgid ""
"Permitting only manual refreshes is a 3 stage process with the above being "
"the first stage. The second stage is to connect the interface, effectively "
"granting permission for refresh management while the third is to set the "
"following _core_ system setting:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/snapd-control-interface.md:29
msgid "sudo snap set system refresh.timer=managed\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/snapd-control-interface.md:32
msgid ""
"The last step activates the manual-only refresh option, skipping upcoming "
"refresh attempts. These values are rechecked and reconfirmed before every "
"future refresh attempt. If any of the steps stop being true, the snap "
"refresh proceeds."
msgstr ""

